    {
      "property_id": "PROP-6a4369e9-inv-047",
      "review_verdict": "CONFIRMED_VULNERABILITY",
      "original_classification": "vulnerability",
      "adjusted_severity": "Medium",
      "reviewer_notes": "Code verification: Confirmed infinite loop vulnerability in handle_custody_groups (peerdas_helpers.nim:50-65). The while loop terminates only when HashSet size equals custody_group_count, but all elements are bounded by mod NUMBER_OF_CUSTODY_GROUPS (128). When peer-reported custody_group_count > 128, the loop saturates at 128 elements and never exits. Spec reference: 01e property (file: 01e_PARTIAL_MANUAL_15_109_190_216.json) explicitly requires 'handle_custody_groups must terminate in O(NUMBER_OF_CUSTODY_GROUPS) iterations regardless of the peer-advertised value.' Attacker control: direct. Path type: attacker-triggered. An attacker can trigger this via P2P by advertising custody_group_count > 128 in peer metadata, causing infinite loop when victim calls checkPeerCustody/matchIntersection during data column sync. No validation exists in lookupCgcFromPeer (eth2_network.nim:2506-2514) which directly returns metadata.custody_group_count. Exploitability confirmed via three P2P entry points: request_manager.nim checkPeerCustody (L313-348), matchIntersection (L374-384), and validator_custody.nim checkIntersectingCustody (L128-143). Severity calibration: Single-packet DoS affecting individual nodes that sync with malicious peer. Not network-wide (< 5% threshold for High severity). Maintaining MEDIUM per bug bounty scope severity definitions - affects multiple nodes via single malicious packet but not >5% of network.",
      "spec_reference": "01e_PARTIAL_MANUAL_15_109_190_216.json: 'Peer-reported custody_group_count must be validated against NUMBER_OF_CUSTODY_GROUPS upper bound before use in any loop or data structure sizing. handle_custody_groups must terminate in O(NUMBER_OF_CUSTODY_GROUPS) iterations regardless of the peer-advertised value.'"
    }
  ],
